   "section": "verse1",
   "lyric_key": "verse1",
   "start": 20.0,
   "end": 50.0,
   "text": "The streetlights flicker on an empty road. I'm carrying all the weight of every word you never said. The mirror shows a stranger I don't know, but I still remember how the morning used to glow. They told me I'd break, they told me I'd fall. I swallowed every punch, I took it all. Now I'm standing in the wreckage, asking who I am, and the answer is burning brighter than their plans.",
